    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46032" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑωλ-ίζω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕωλος</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>keep till next day</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ κρέα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					16.761
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				4.2.8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be</i> or <i>become stale</i>, of grain, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.518
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in good
			sense, <i>to be capable of being kept till next day</i>, ib. <i><span class="en">
				713
			</span></i>.</div>
